# box: this file used to expose adb, mtp, ptp, rndis, midi, uvc, accessory and
# audio_source on the USB bus.  All of those are gone.
#
# Why: a host that sees an Android function next to the Apple interface
# classifies the box as an Android device and stops probing for CarPlay.  The
# mixed layout (ffs.adb + ffs.iap2 in configuration 1) was caught in the
# 2026-10-25 field log; see docs/evidence/native-iap2-interface-2026-10-25.md.
#
# carplay_supervisor.sh owns configuration 1 now.  Nothing in init may touch
# b.1, because a symlink here and a symlink there race each other.
#
# adbd still runs, as a TCP daemon on 5555.  That is the only remote channel
# besides the UART console, so do not add "stop adbd" anywhere in this file.

on property:sys.usb.config=none && property:sys.usb.configfs=1
    write /config/usb_gadget/g1/UDC "none"
    setprop sys.usb.ffs.ready 0
    setprop sys.usb.ffs.mtp.ready 0
    write /config/usb_gadget/g1/bDeviceClass 0
    write /config/usb_gadget/g1/bDeviceSubClass 0
    write /config/usb_gadget/g1/bDeviceProtocol 0
    setprop sys.usb.state ${sys.usb.config}

on property:init.svc.adbd=stopped
    setprop sys.usb.ffs.ready 0
